.TH EXECAC 1
.SH NAME
execac \- run a command on an application core
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B execac
[
.B -c
.I core
]
.I command
[
.I arg ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Execac
runs
.I command
with its arguments on the application core
.IR core ,
on any free one by default
(see
.IR execac (2)).
A
.I command
without a leading
.L /
or
.L ./
is looked up in
.BR /bin .
The application cores are those set aside by
.B *nixac
in
.IR plan9.ini (8).
.SH EXAMPLES
On a machine booted with
.BR *nixac=1 ,
four processors:
.IP
.EX
% execac -c 3 rc -c 'cat /proc/$pid/core'
          3
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/cmd/execac.c
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR execac (2),
.IR proc (3)
